.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-DELETE-NAMESPACE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-delete-namespace \- delete a namespace under an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam delete-namespace
.BR \-\-account\-id | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes the namespace identified by \fIACCOUNTID\fR/\fINAME\fR via the
eam service's
.I delete-namespace
action.
.PP
The caller must be a global administrator, or hold account-scoped
administrator privileges on \fIACCOUNTID\fR (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1)).
.PP
Every user grant referencing this namespace must first be revoked (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access (1)) -
the server rejects the request with \fIHTTP 409\fR otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account\-id " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Account the namespace belongs to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the namespace to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The namespace was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller
lacks administrator privileges on the account, no namespace with that
name exists under the account, or the namespace still has user grants
(\fIHTTP 409\fR). If the failure was an expired or invalid session
(\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam delete-namespace \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --name staging
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-namespaces (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access (1)
